# CODEOWNERS — narrow ownership for policy-sensitive paths only.
#
# NO blanket `* @GoodOlClint` line, deliberately. Code-level review is
# claude-bot's job via .github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml; a blanket
# owner would require operator approval on every PR, which makes that review
# advisory in practice and puts the human back in the loop for routine work.
# The sibling repo removed its blanket line on 2026-04-19 for exactly this
# reason.
#
# The paths below are NOT arbitrary: they are the review prompt's own
# "You defer to @GoodOlClint" list (.github/review-prompt.md), expressed as
# ownership so the deferral is ENFORCED rather than requested. The reviewer
# is instructed to defer on these; CODEOWNERS makes it structural. Keep the
# two lists in sync — if one grows, so does the other.

# --- Architecture: the decision is the operator's, even when the code is fine
/docs/decisions/                            @GoodOlClint
/Sources/athena/Server/OpenAPISpec.swift    @GoodOlClint
/Sources/athena/Server/NativeAPIDTO.swift   @GoodOlClint

# --- Substrate pins and dependency surface (license / supply-chain)
/Package.swift                              @GoodOlClint
/Package.resolved                           @GoodOlClint

# --- Security posture: auth/RBAC, at-rest encryption, signing/notarization
/Sources/AthenaServerKit/Auth.swift         @GoodOlClint
/Sources/AthenaStore/                       @GoodOlClint
/deploy/                                    @GoodOlClint

# --- Release / versioning: appVersion is the SSOT and bumps only in a release
/Sources/athena/Athena.swift                @GoodOlClint

# --- The rules themselves, and the machinery that enforces them.
# Highest-privilege files in the repo: whoever edits these edits the reviewer.
/AGENTS.md                                  @GoodOlClint
/CLAUDE.md                                  @GoodOlClint
/.github/                                   @GoodOlClint
